    <statement><p>Calculate the derivative using the appropriate rule or combination of rules.
<me>g(z)=\frac{z^{2}-5z+6}{z+4}\frac{z^{2}+7z+12}{z-3}</me></p>
<p><m>g'(z) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2z+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>g(z)=\frac{z^{2}-5z+6}{z+4}\frac{z^{2}+7z+12}{z-3}=\frac{\left(z-3\right)\mathopen{}\left(z-2\right)}{z+4}\frac{\left(z+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(z+4\right)}{z-3}.</me>
<m>g(z)=\left(z-2\right)\mathopen{}\left(z+3\right)</m>, assuming <m>z \ne 3</m> and <m>z \ne -4</m>, whence
<me>g'(z)=(z+3)(1)+(z-2)(1)=2z+1.</me>


</solution>
